<%- include('../../partials/head') %>
<header class="page-head">
  <div><h1>Inventory</h1><p class="muted">One-time import of the inventory spreadsheet.</p></div>
</header>
<%- include('../_tabs') %>

<div class="grid-2 grid-wide-left">
  <section class="card">
    <h2>Upload the spreadsheet</h2>
    <% if (hasPlan) { %>
      <div class="flash flash-info">You have an import preview waiting. <a href="/inventory/import/preview">Open the preview</a>, or upload again to start over.</div>
    <% } %>
    <form method="post" action="/inventory/import" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="form">
      <%- csrfField %>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Excel file (.xlsx)</span>
        <input type="file" name="file" accept=".xlsx,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet" required>
      </label>
      <div><button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary"><%- icon('upload') %><span>Read file and preview</span></button></div>
    </form>
    <p class="muted small">Nothing is saved until you confirm on the next page. The file itself is deleted as soon as it has been read.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2><%- icon('lock') %> What is never imported</h2>
    <ul class="small">
      <li>Any column whose header contains <strong>Password</strong>, <strong>Pass</strong> or <strong>PIN</strong>. These are skipped before a single value is read, and are never saved, logged or shown. That includes a column called "1Password", so 1Password access has to be added by hand.</li>
      <li>Columns with no header, or whose header looks like data (for example an email address).</li>
      <li>Everything on "Old Gmail" except User, Gmail-ID and Status.</li>
      <li>The "Inventory Breakdown" and "Service Accounts" sheets (duplicates).</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What is imported</h3>
    <ul class="small">
      <li><strong>PK Team / Writers:</strong> people, laptops (two serials in one cell = two laptops), Gmail/Outlook/Apple IDs and apps marked Done as access entries.</li>
      <li><strong>Left:</strong> people marked as Left, with their laptops as Spare (or Sold).</li>
      <li><strong>User Inventory:</strong> each person's equipment as assets or stock.</li>
      <li><strong>Inventory / Demage / Sold:</strong> counted items, damaged quantities, sold laptops.</li>
      <li><strong>Old Gmail:</strong> Gmail accounts (Deleted = Removed).</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small muted">People are matched by name and assets by serial number, so importing again does not create duplicates.</p>
  </section>
</div>
<%- include('../../partials/foot') %>
